+# Migration to Managed Postgres / Managed Redis
+
+Overview
+--------
+Guidance and checklist for migrating the in-cluster DB/queue to managed services (RDS/Cloud SQL, Managed Redis/Kafka).
+
+Steps
+1. Provision managed Postgres (multi-AZ) and managed Redis (or Kafka topics) with required capacity.
+2. Provision pgbouncer (or managed connection pool) and configure secrets for app usage.
+3. Update environment variables:
+   - DATABASE_URL -> managed postgres endpoint (use Vault for secret injection)
+   - REDIS_URL -> managed Redis connection string
+4. Deploy `ops/db/check_managed_services.py` in CI to validate connectivity.
+5. Switch evidence-worker to `ops/queue/worker_postgres.py`.
+6. Run migration:
+   - Export data from local Postgres (pg_dump)
+   - Import into managed Postgres
+7. Validate end-to-end signing/indexing in staging before swapping production traffic.
+
+Rollback
+- Keep backup of local index and ensure you can revert DB URL quickly via CI/ConfigMap.
+
